Z||000004||Cliff Pennock||01-05-2000||07:03 PM||||The risks are that there are several ways to embed scripts inside HTML that can do all kinds of scary stuff to the server.<P>But besides it being a security risk, if someone for instance forgets a closing HTML tag, or has one too many, it will mess up the page alltogether.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Phil||01-05-2000||07:27 PM||||Maybe it's because I'm an old gas passer but I seem to find that people tend to do things on a computer not because it's necessary but rather  because they can. Do we really need flashing lights and the like on an informational site. Kinda think it would start looking like "Crazy Dan's Used Cars" Come on down-no money down-no one turned down<BR>The smilies are just an example, they are somewhat cute but are sometimes over used and lose any effect  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||FieroMike||01-05-2000||07:50 PM||||Phil,<BR>Good point, it's definately not NECESSARY.  However, everyone isn't an old geezer like you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  J/K  I would agree in the tech forum, but if you are going to have a general forum you have to be more leniant.  Also, if the post/topic doesn't interest you or it looks like young, useless information... don't read it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Besides, it's just fun to mess around...||||reg||12
Z||000007||theogre||01-07-2000||07:29 PM||||Cliff is right. the HTML support in Ultimate is not all that reliable. Other forums that enable it have to constantly fix things and delete threads that are hosed.<P>It also opens the whole system up to maggots who just have to trash things to be anal. The recent "winnner" of a ZDnet hack site test did so by embedding code into a text box on a web page. All it took was a single box that wasn't coded just right in the site.<P>Personally I find the other forums that allow it, like the NoWonder PC help site, don't benifit from it. Most messages with HTML end up being really annoying to read.||||reg||1
